      "content": "I see what you're saying. It sounds like you're leaning more towards the idea that human agency and government intervention are the most important factors here, rather than the technology itself. \n\nSome people would argue that the tech moves so fast that the \"steering\" you mentioned is actually an illusion—that by the time a policy is passed, the economic reality has already changed. Do you think the \"technological inevitability\" argument is just a way for big tech companies to avoid accountability for the social disruptions they cause?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
